{"name":"Blue et une Nuit","hex":"#0652ff","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"},{"term":"une","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Uneme."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/une"}],"entries":[{"title":"Une","blocks":[{"text":"Une is a municipality in the Cundinamarca Department, Colombia, located in the Eastern Province. It is situated 27 miles southeast of Bogotá, the country's capital."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/UNE_CUNDINAMARCA_FOTOGRAFIA_AEREA_DE_CAMINOS.png/330px-UNE_CUNDINAMARCA_FOTOGRAFIA_AEREA_DE_CAMINOS.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Une","wikidata":"Q1577653"},{"title":"Nuit","blocks":[{"text":"Nuit is a goddess in Thelema, a Western esoteric quasi-religion. Nuit is the speaker in the first chapter of The Book of the Law, the sacred text written or received in 1904 by Aleister Crowley. Nuit is based on the Ancient Egyptian sky goddess Nut, who in Egyptian mythology arches over her brother/husband, Geb. She is usually depicted as a naked woman who is covered with stars."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nuit","wikidata":"Q7068814"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue","wikidata":"Q1088"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/UNE_CUNDINAMARCA_FOTOGRAFIA_AEREA_DE_CAMINOS.png/500px-UNE_CUNDINAMARCA_FOTOGRAFIA_AEREA_DE_CAMINOS.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/UNE_CUNDINAMARCA_FOTOGRAFIA_AEREA_DE_CAMINOS.png/500px-UNE_CUNDINAMARCA_FOTOGRAFIA_AEREA_DE_CAMINOS.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AUNE_CUNDINAMARCA_FOTOGRAFIA_AEREA_DE_CAMINOS.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Plaza_de_toros_de_Une_%2801%29.jpg/330px-Plaza_de_toros_de_Une_%2801%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Plaza_de_toros_de_Une_%2801%29.jpg/330px-Plaza_de_toros_de_Une_%2801%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Leopoldo Romero Cubillos Bullring","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APlaza_de_toros_de_Une_(01).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Municipio_de_Une-Cundinamarca.jpg/330px-Municipio_de_Une-Cundinamarca.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https: